            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='3867' id='38' type-v2='text' w='99308' x='538' y='28511'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='15'>The figures above summarise the overall scale of competition between 2020 and 2024. During this period, drivers scored more than 10,000 points in total, achieved over 100 race wins, and stood on the podium more than 300 times.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='15'>At the same time, more than 300 races ended in retirement. These DNFs highlight how reliability remained a critical factor alongside pure performance.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='5978' id='39' type-v2='text' w='97692' x='77' y='32511'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff0000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='24'>Reliability Analysis</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='15'>In Formula 1, speed alone is not enough. A car that frequently fails to finish races will struggle to compete for championships, regardless of its pace. Reliability issues can be caused by mechanical problems, accidents, or other on-track incidents.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='15'>This section examines which constructors and drivers experienced the highest number of DNFs between 2020 and 2024. Understanding these patterns helps explain why some strong performances still resulted in lost points and missed opportunities.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='8733' id='40' name='Reliability by Team' show-title='false' w='51385' x='0' y='39156' />
        <zone h='1422' id='41' name='Reliability by Team' pane-specification-id='0' param='[federated.0dtt1j818oxqr018n4mrk0chk9af].[none:status_category:nk]' type-v2='color' w='11846' x='37385' y='43889' />
        <zone h='9000' id='42' name='Reliability by Driver' show-title='false' w='46769' x='51692' y='39133' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='4067' id='43' type-v2='text' w='99692' x='77' y='47467'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#59a14f' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='24'>Wins &amp; Podium Finishes</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='15'>While total points show overall consistency, race wins and podium finishes highlight peak performance. This section compares how many races drivers won and how often they finished in the top three between 2020 and 2024.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='8067' id='44' name='Wins vs Podiums' show-title='false' w='98154' x='-154' y='52244' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='4711' id='47' type-v2='text' w='98538' x='538' y='59822'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff9da7' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='25'>Average Positions Gained</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='15'>This chart shows how many positions drivers gained on average from their starting grid position. A higher number means the driver was good at overtaking or recovering during races. Negative values mean the driver usually finished worse than they started.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='10467' id='48' name='Average Position Gained' show-title='false' w='98308' x='462' y='64311' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='4289' id='49' type-v2='text' w='95923' x='1231' y='74600'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#f28e2b' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='25'>Points Progression Across Seasons</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='15'>This line chart shows how the top drivers accumulated points from 2020 to 2024. It helps us see consistency, breakthrough seasons, and how the competitive order changed over the five-year period.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='12400' id='50' name='Points Progression' show-title='false' w='91923' x='3308' y='78667' />
        <zone h='4689' id='51' name='Points Progression' pane-specification-id='0' param='[federated.0dtt1j818oxqr018n4mrk0chk9af].[none:driver_name:nk]' type-v2='color' w='11231' x='85615' y='79222' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='6889' id='52' type-v2='text' w='92154' x='5385' y='91889'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#5500ff' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='25'>Conclusion</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='15'>Between 2020 and 2024, Formula 1 showed a clear competitive hierarchy. A small group of drivers and teams consistently scored the majority of points, while reliability remained a decisive factor. Mechanical failures and accidents cost valuable points even to strong performers.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='15'>This dashboard highlights that success in Formula 1 depends not only on speed, but also on consistency and the ability to finish races. The combination of championship results and reliability data gives a more complete picture of performance during these five seasons.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='1444' id='53' name='Reliability by Driver' param='[federated.0dtt1j818oxqr018n4mrk0chk9af].[none:year:qk]' type-v2='filter' values='database' w='12308' x='84615' y='37711' />
